## 7. Ruff Plugin Analysis (Added `just cheap`)

### 7.1 Plugins Added to `pyproject.toml`

| Plugin | Rule | Rationale | Status |
|--------|------|-----------|--------|
| `FA` | flake8-future-annotations | Aspirational — won't fire at py313 but documents intent | Added |
| `PT` | flake8-pytest-style | Catches `@pytest.mark.asyncio`, fixture patterns, assertion style | Added |
| `BLE` | flake8-blind-except | Catches bare `except:` without logging | Added, `BLE001` globally ignored (all instances log) |
| `TD` | flake8-todos | TODO/FIXME formatting consistency | Added |
| `LOG` | flake8-logging | structlog usage patterns (LOG009: getLogger, LOG015: f-strings) | Added |

### 7.2 Remaining Ruff Violations (After Config)

After enabling PT, BLE, TD, LOG, 17 violations remain, all from `PT`:

| Rule | Count | File(s) | Description |
|------|-------|---------|-------------|
| `PT017` | 8 | `test_sftp_server.py` | Assertions on exception `e` in `except` block; should use `pytest.raises()` |
| `PT022` | 4 | `conftest.py`, `test_ca_ops.py`, `test_queries.py` | Fixtures use `yield` without teardown; should use `return` |
| `PT018` | 1 | `test_http_upload.py` | Compound assertion `assert A and B` should be two assertions |
| `PT011` | 3 | `test_drv_parser.py`, `test_signing.py` | `pytest.raises(ValueError)` too broad; should add `match=` |
| `PT006` | 1 | `test_types_derivation.py` | Parametrize first arg should be `tuple`, not `str` |

These are all legitimate quality issues but can be addressed separately. The PT022 and PT018 are the easiest fixes.

### 7.3 Per-File Ignore Configuration

```toml
[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]
"tests/**" = ["ERA001", "RUF059", "F401", "T201", "ARG001"]
"tests/ai/**" = ["ERA001", "RUF059", "F401", "T201", "ARG001", "BLE001"]
"tests/conftest.py" = ["ERA001", "RUF059", "F401", "T201", "ARG001", "BLE001"]
```

The `tests/ai/` and `conftest.py` entries suppress BLE for test helper scripts where bare `except` is intentional (error recovery in `rmtree_robust`, script-style error handling in AI tests).

### 7.4 Rules Evaluated But Not Added

| Plugin | Why Not Added |
|--------|--------------|
| `EM` | Too noisy — production code uses f-strings in exceptions by design (~50 violations) |
| `ANN` | Too noisy for tests and production (`-> None` on every function) |
| `D`/`DOC` | pydocstyle is too opinionated about docstring formats |
| `S` | flake8-bandit is useful but noisy; would need extensive suppressions |
| `PL` | Pylint comprehensive but extremely noisy for this codebase |
| `COM` | Commas already handled by `ruff format` |
| `C90` | Cyclomatic complexity; useful but would need a higher threshold |
| `SLF` | Private member access; pynixd accesses private members internally |
| `PGH` | Pygrep hooks would be useful for custom checks but ruff doesn't support custom hooks |
| `ISC` | Implicit string concatenation; would need review |
| `ICN` | Import conventions; current aliases are intentional |
| `DTZ` | datetimez; codebase uses `time.monotonic()` not `datetime.now()`

